{"schema_version":1,"course":"tourist-fr","unit":"food-and-getting-around","language":"en","target_language":"fr","phrases":[{"concept":"one-coffee-please","text":{"Latn":"One coffee, please"}},{"concept":"where-is-the-bathroom","text":{"Latn":"Where is the bathroom?"}}],"glosses":[{"lemma":"fr:un","gloss":"one, a","note":"Un (masculine), une (feminine)."},{"lemma":"fr:cafe","gloss":"coffee","note":"Also a café as a place. On its own, \"un café\" is a small, strong black coffee."},{"lemma":"fr:si","gloss":"if","note":"Becomes s' before \"il\": s'il."},{"lemma":"fr:vous","gloss":"you","note":"The polite and the plural \"you\"; \"tu\" is the informal singular."},{"lemma":"fr:plaire","gloss":"to please","note":"\"S'il vous plaît\" is literally \"if it pleases you\", the standard way to say \"please\"."},{"lemma":"fr:ou","gloss":"where","note":"With an accent: \"ou\" without one means \"or\"."},{"lemma":"fr:etre","gloss":"to be"},{"lemma":"fr:le","gloss":"the","note":"Le (masculine), la (feminine), les (plural)."},{"lemma":"fr:toilettes","gloss":"bathroom, toilet","note":"Always plural in French."}]}
